ce annotation, restricting Spring Boot's auto-configuration to the Couchbase data layer for focused repository tests. It configures Couchbase templates, repositories, and client factories, and contributes the runtime hints these test slices need to run under native image.\"\n```\n\n`language` stays absent — this is a plain Java module, not language-specific.\n\n★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\nSpring Boot 4 restructured its once-monolithic `spring-boot-project` into dozens of single-purpose Gradle modules under `spring-boot/module/<name>/`, each publishing its own jar, sources jar, and javadoc jar to Maven Central under matching coordinates. That's why every sibling entry in this repo follows the exact same three-URL shape — it's not a per-library guess, it's a structural property of how the whole project is built and released.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nWould you like to grant Edit permission for this file so I can apply the change now, or would you prefer to make the edit yourself with these values?\n\nEXIT_CODE: 0\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1791066896377}}
